ent. Record maintainer resolution for every critique item. Then DRAFT, HOLD for review, and MERGE an ADR that mandates one canonical private binding and atomic consumer migration.\n\n## Scope\n\n- new ADR allocated through `docs/adr/.numbers`\n- `docs/api-stability.md` and architecture/reuse guidance\n- enforcement/review guidance or a mechanical guard identified by the ADR\n\n## Testing\n\nAdd a policy/documentation check or deterministic enforcement test specified by the ADR; verify existing public facade, wire-schema, and persisted-event contract tests remain unaffected.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] RESEARCH contains a numbered critique of ADR 0016, ADR 0083, ADR 0092, and prior split-shim guidance; each item has a recorded maintainer resolution.\n- [ ] The merged ADR defines one canonical binding after private moves and atomic source/test/string/dynamic/monkeypatch migration.\n- [ ] The ADR distinguishes valid public facades, MCP wire schemas, event readers, and persisted-data migrations from internal-only shims.\n- [ ] The ADR requires a durable review or mechanical recurrence-prevention mechanism and names its evidence.\n- [ ] The policy check/enforcement evidence passes without breaking the preserved public/wire/event contracts.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"docs/adr/.numbers","reason":"allocate the next ADR number through the established mechanism"},{"path":"docs/adr","reason":"add the governing no-internal-shim ADR"},{"path":"docs/api-stability.md","reason":"align private/public compatibility guidance"},{"path":"docs/architecture.md","reason":"align internal move/re-export guidance"},{"path":"tests","reason":"add or update policy/enforcement evidence required by ADR"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["parent","6640-ac11-5c55-46b5"],["relates_to","0869-d459-7b1a-4981"],["relates_to","85a3-2999-cf50-4f25"],["relates_to","9db7-